The Mercedes-Benz Vito 113 CDi is primarily associated with the W639 generation (2003-2014), including the facelifted models from 2010-2014. It typically features a 2.1-litre 4-cylinder turbo-diesel engine producing 100 kW (134 hp) and 310 Nm of torque. It was available with both manual and automatic transmissions and rear-wheel drive, with some 4x4 variants also existing. It was offered in various body styles including panel van, crew cab, and passenger versions (Traveliner/Combi).

